{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1791141761,"nonce":"MRL3L++GmsagJR/J/RVgo3m14k4=","message":"Changed to CSS semantics, and the change was smaller than the report\nimplied.\n\nBlinc already counted line-height against the FONT SIZE nearly\neverywhere: EstimatedTextMeasurer, FontTextMeasurer::estimate_size, the\nhit tester, the code editor and the rich-text renderer all compute\nfont_size * line_height. Exactly one place disagreed,\nblinc_text/src/layout.rs, which multiplied by the face's own\nline_height_px (ascent + descent + gap). So the font-backed layout\nengine disagreed not only with CSS but with its own fallback.\n\nThat one line now counts against the font size.\n\nMeasured before and after, at font_size 100 with line_height 1.0:\n  System / SansSerif (Helvetica): 100.00 -\u003e 100.00, unchanged, because\n  its natural line height is exactly 1em. That is why this hid for so\n  long.\n  Monospace: 113.28 -\u003e 100.00, so monospace lines were 13.3% taller than\n  asked for and are now correct.\n\nVerified on screen too: in the capture scene the monospace boxes get\nshorter and the rows tighten, baselines still align between sans and\nmono at the same size, and button text stays centred.\n\nPrerequisite for e974c36 cleared: SF Pro's natural line height is about\n1.19 to 1.21em, so under the old semantics adopting it would have made\nevery line roughly a fifth taller. It will now measure font_size *\nline_height like everything else.","files":null}]}